# Security headers on every response the site serves. At build the Cloudflare
# adapter puts its own rule above this one, immutable Cache-Control for
# /_astro/*, and would skip it if a rule here set Cache-Control on that path,
# so nothing below does. See docs/routing-and-deploy.md §5.
#
# HSTS: a year, with subdomains, since www and media are both served over HTTPS.
#
# The CSP holds only the directives that need no hashes. A script-src or
# style-src would have to hash the five inline scripts and the inlined
# stylesheets, which change with every edit to them, and allow the `style`
# attributes that carry the tile spans.
#
# Permissions-Policy names only features Chrome recognises: an unknown one is
# logged as a console error. fullscreen stays allowed for the demo video.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
